  "solution": {
    "text": "Rate of electrophilic aromatic substitution is effected by group/s already present. If they <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>-</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>-</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>-</mo></mrow></mfenced></math> are ring activating and ortho, para directing due to +R and +H effects reactivity is more but if they <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>-</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> are ring deactivating and meta directing groups due to -R and -H effects reactivity decreases. <br/>Here reactivity order is 3 &gt; 1 &gt; 4 &gt; 2."
